{
  "number": 41,
  "title": "Move existing ventures onto the structured layout (EE-086 stage 3)",
  "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"tchjhnsn\"} -->\n_Requested by **Torian**_\n\nStage 3 of the venture project structure (EE-086), stacked on #40.\n\n## What it does\n\n- **`naive upgrade --layout structured [--owner <person>] [--check]`** moves an existing venture onto the structured layout: packages into `knowledge/`; `provenance.jsonl`, `naive.config.json`, `sources.json` and `.release/` into `meta/`; `profile.md` to `README.md`; and a flat org chart into `venture.json`. Routes, citations and the provenance log keep their logical paths, so no alias is needed. Opt-in, so `schema/upgrades.json` is unchanged.\n- **The example ventures are converted** with `git mv`, so their history follows them.\n- **Org chart check** (`schema/structure.mjs`): for a structured venture, a function is a package or names the packages it merges; a package belongs to one function; `decisions/`, `evidence/` and `raw/` stay venture-wide. Meta files left in `knowledge/` are errors.\n- **Fixes found on the way:**\n  - `mentura init` passes `--layout` and `--owner` through.\n  - Init no longer makes stray folders.\n  - Route groups find `knowledge/(group)/AGENTS.md`.\n  - Several walkers had been remapping paths that were already physical.\n  - `check-provenance` accepts a folder entity.\n- **`NAIVE_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`**: the venture search stops there, and `test.mjs` sets it to the checkout's parent. Without it, a checkout kept in a venture's `repo/` folder let a bare `naive upgrade` in the tests act on that real venture. That happened once while this was built; the venture was restored.\n\n## Docs\n\n- **Project structure:** the three folders and a new Functions section.\n- **Upgrading:** the layout move, with commands the docs test runs as written.\n- **Installation** paths and the 0.4.0 guide.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\n- Renaming the 38 routes whose names differ from their paths, so every route is its path. That waits for the stage 4 router trim.\n- The plugin's write hook (stage 4).\n\n## Test\n\n`node test.mjs`: all passing.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
